From d766fdb2be2143410427136e29dbf1e5b7e464d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 15:33:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(maic): remove the OpenMAIC brand from the embedded
 classroom
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The embed still announced itself as a second product: the browser tab said
OpenMAIC, the home hero showed its wordmark over a tagline spelling the name
out, the footer read "OpenMAIC Open Source Project", and the classroom sidebar,
PBL workspace header and access-code gate each showed the mark again.

lib/brand/brand-config.ts already was the one place a brand is declared, and
three surfaces read it. The rest hardcoded the logo path and the string beside
it. Those now read it too; the config defaults to the host product and every
field is overridable through NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_* (inlined at build time).

The brand also left the machine, where removing a logo would not have reached:
a User-Agent sent to every SearXNG instance, an MM-API-Source header sent to
MiniMax, open.maic.chat printed on every exported video cover, and .maic.zip on
every course a user saves. Import is unaffected — the picker takes .zip and
never compared against that constant.

Outbound links: open-in-chat.tsx (six, to ChatGPT/Claude/T3/Scira/v0/Cursor) and
sources.tsx were dead files and are deleted; Settings' three Baidu doc anchors
and the docsUrl behind them are gone. What stays clickable is internal.

80 translated strings across 13 languages, each rewritten in its own language.
home.slogan and settings.viewDocs lost their last readers and are removed — 1798
keys where the pin said 1800, hence the pin bump.

Two wire identifiers renamed across 14 files: data-maic-element-id ->
data-element-id, X-OpenMAIC-Element-Reference-Accepted ->
X-Element-Reference-Accepted.

Left deliberately: @openmaic/* package names, OPENMAIC_*/NEXT_PUBLIC_MAIC_* env
vars, maic-connector, and comments — none visible to a reader, and renaming them
buys upstream conflicts for nothing. LICENSE untouched; MIT wants the notice in
the distribution, not the UI.

Verified on the running container: title DeepWitya, zero case-insensitive maic
matches and zero external links on / and /workspace, old assets 404. tsc clean,
eslint clean, upstream check-i18n-keys green at 13 locales, contract check green,
image builds. cover-config.test.ts also gained the th-TH row it had been missing
since Thai joined the Locale union, which had left tsc red on it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
